        },
        "review-18": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Walter N.",
            "reviewer_age": 69,
            "date": "Aug 2",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Bone-on-bone and this still helps.",
            "body": "<p>My orthopaedic surgeon told me I am bone-on-bone and the only real fix is a replacement. I am not ready for surgery so I am managing. Waldon does not fix the cartilage — nothing will — but it takes the edge off the grinding sensation enough that I can function through a full day.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 1",
            "image_2_label": "Week 8",
            "tags": "bone-on-bone,management",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-19": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Helen G.",
            "reviewer_age": 55,
            "date": "Jul 20",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Chasing my toddler grandchildren again.",
            "body": "<p>Two toddler grandchildren who do not slow down. I had been sitting out the park trips for months. Started Waldon and within three weeks I was back on the playground with them. The look on their faces when grandma got on the slide was worth it.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Before",
            "image_2_label": "Week 5",
            "tags": "active,family",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-20": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Arthur B.",
            "reviewer_age": 77,
            "date": "Jul 7",
            "rating": 4,
            "headline": "Took three weeks but the wait was worth it.",
            "body": "<p>I did not feel much the first two weeks and nearly returned it. My wife convinced me to give it another week. Week three something shifted — the morning stiffness that had been constant for two years was just gone one morning. I am glad I waited.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 1",
            "image_2_label": "Week 4",
            "tags": "patience,morning-stiffness",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-21": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Shirley P.",
            "reviewer_age": 62,
            "date": "Jun 25",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Back to walking 10,000 steps.",
            "body": "<p>My step count had dropped to under 4,000 because every walk ended in pain. I started wearing Waldon on walks and built back up gradually. Hit 10,000 steps last Tuesday for the first time in 18 months. I cried a little, not going to lie.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 2",
            "image_2_label": "Week 10",
            "tags": "walking,fitness",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-22": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Raymond J.",
            "reviewer_age": 68,
            "date": "Jun 12",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Reduced my pain medication.",
            "body": "<p>I was taking two ibuprofen every morning just to get moving. By week four I was down to one. By week six I stopped altogether on most days. I am not saying it is a replacement for medication — but for me it reduced how much I needed. Talk to your doctor, obviously.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 2",
            "image_2_label": "Week 6",
            "tags": "pain-relief,medication",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-23": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Virginia H.",
            "reviewer_age": 57,
            "date": "May 30",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Works under compression tights too.",
            "body": "<p>I already wear compression tights for circulation and was not sure if layering would work. I wear the Waldon sleeve under the tights and it is perfectly comfortable — no bunching, no pressure points. The combined effect on swelling has been remarkable.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 1",
            "image_2_label": "Week 5",
            "tags": "layering,circulation",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-24": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Carl W.",
            "reviewer_age": 72,
            "date": "May 17",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Standing for my grandson's graduation.",
            "body": "<p>Three-hour outdoor graduation. Standing most of the time. Knew my knee would struggle. Wore Waldon and was genuinely fine. Drove home four hours afterwards. Only minor stiffness by bedtime. A year ago that day would have wiped me out for a week.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Event day",
            "image_2_label": "Next morning",
            "tags": "events,standing",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-25": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Mildred C.",
            "reviewer_age": 76,
            "date": "May 4",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Gifted one to my sister. She loves it too.",
            "body": "<p>Bought one for myself, and when my sister visited and saw how I was moving she asked about it. Ordered her one on the spot. She called me two weeks later to say thank you. Now we are both wearing them and comparing notes like we are in a club.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 1",
            "image_2_label": "Week 6",
            "tags": "gift,family",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-26": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Eugene D.",
            "reviewer_age": 61,
            "date": "Apr 22",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Survived the holiday shopping season.",
            "body": "<p>I work in a department store and the holiday season is brutal — six hours on hard floors daily for six weeks. Last year I finished December in real pain. This year I wore Waldon every shift. Finished the season with manageable tiredness but zero of the joint pain I had before. Night and day.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 1",
            "image_2_label": "Week 6",
            "tags": "standing,retail",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-27": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Phyllis K.",
            "reviewer_age": 66,
            "date": "Apr 9",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "First thing I put on, last thing I take off.",
            "body": "<p>I put it on before I get out of bed in the morning — that is how much difference those first ten minutes make. My knee is warm and supported before I take a single step. It has just become part of the routine. Cannot imagine mornings without it.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Week 1",
            "image_2_label": "Month 2",
            "tags": "morning,routine",
            "verified": true
          }
        },
        "review-28": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "reviewer_name": "Bernard L.",
            "reviewer_age": 64,
            "date": "Mar 28",
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Finally took a proper holiday.",
            "body": "<p>We had cancelled two holidays in the past two years because I could not face the amount of walking. Booked a week in Portugal after two months with Waldon. Walked cobblestone streets for seven days. My wife keeps saying she has her husband back. That one hit hard.</p>",
            "image_1_label": "Before trip",
            "image_2_label": "Day 7",
            "tags": "travel,walking",
            "verified": true
          }
        }
